the struggle of finding workers for  certain business is really continuing in  and around las vegas tonight victoria  saha telling us why a restaurant has to  close their doors twice a week now  so their current workers are not  overwhelmed  the kitchen staff at juan's flaming  fanitas in the southwest valley and  tropicana near fort apache  is busy at work doing the best they can  with limited staff  we've asked them to pick up the extra  shifts to work the extra hours and  they've more than obliged to do that  because they want to see us continue to  grow  now on mondays and tuesdays the kitchen  and restaurant will have their lights  off  give them an opportunity to have some  downtime and spend some time with their  family  earlier this week they put out a  statement saying they will close two  days out of the week  to lessen the burden on their exhausted  staff probably the past six months  we've had very minimal applicants coming  in so  that's kind of what's led to it's not  just a couple weeks of picking up extra  it's been continued months  of them working those extra ships to  give you a better understanding of the  staffing shortage here  the manager says on average they used to  have 110 employees  right now they're down to 85. sometimes  having to bring in staff from their  henderson location to help kitchen  manager claudio carlos is one of the  staff that decided to stick around  everybody working more time so now he  never got time for spending time with  his  family and everything that was  something hard for everybody he says  he's staying because the owners are  valuing their staff with the two days  off  the restaurant has a referral program if  an employee brings in a new staff member  they each get 250 dollars victoria zaha  8 news now  victoria thanks now they don't know when  they'll reopen again on mondays and  tuesdays they need people they're hoping  as soon as they are fully staffed they  can get back to normal business hours  if you would like to apply link up on  our website 8newsnow.com a lot of jobs  out there
 

